    <!-- one‑paragraph (full description) -->
    <div class="lead">
      <strong>DataLens</strong> is a lightweight, privacy‑first CSV analysis dashboard that runs entirely in your browser. 
      Upload a CSV file and instantly explore statistics, quality warnings, interactive SVG charts (bar, line, pie, scatter), 
      a fully searchable and sortable table, plus intelligent insights — all wrapped in a polished glassmorphic interface 
      with dark/light theme support. No server, no data sharing, just instant analytics.
    </div>

    <!-- two‑column: features + tech / shortcuts -->
    <div class="grid-2col">
      <!-- left: features -->
      <div class="feature-block">
        <h3><i>⚡</i> Core capabilities</h3>
        <ul class="feature-list">
          <li>Drag‑and‑drop CSV parsing (quoted fields, comma‑separated)</li>
          <li>Auto‑statistics: row count, missing %, duplicates, column types</li>
          <li>Quality warnings (high nulls, constant columns, unique IDs)</li>
          <li>4 recommended charts: bar, line, pie, scatter – rendered as SVG</li>
          <li>Global search + per‑column filters &amp; sortable table</li>
          <li>Custom chart builder with X/Y axis selection</li>
          <li>Export visible/filtered data as CSV</li>
          <li>Persistent theme preference (dark / light) via localStorage</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- right: stack + shortcuts + usage -->
      <div class="feature-block">
        <h3><i>🧩</i> Stack &amp; UX</h3>
